.\" man/man3/Docv::Viewer::Picker::Outline.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Viewer::Picker::Outline" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Viewer::Picker::Outline \- Items folded into groups by the name prefixes they share, for the page search: \fB\%abrt\-cli\fR and \fB\%abrt\-dump\-oops\fR under \fB\%abrt\fR, and \fB\%abrt\-dump\-oops\fR and \fB\%abrt\-dump\-xorg\fR under \fB\%abrt\-dump\fR within it.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Viewer::Picker::Outline\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Items folded into groups by the name prefixes they share, for the
page search: \fB\%abrt\-cli\fR and \fB\%abrt\-dump\-oops\fR under \fB\%abrt\fR, and
\fB\%abrt\-dump\-oops\fR and \fB\%abrt\-dump\-xorg\fR under \fB\%abrt\-dump\fR within it.
.PP
An item\(aqs \fB\%Item#key\fR splits into tokens at runs of \fB\%SEPARATORS\fR
(\fB\%::\fR counts once). A prefix of whole tokens shared by at least
\fB\%MIN_GROUP\fR items becomes a group; a group with a single subgroup and
no items of its own takes that subgroup\(aqs prefix instead. Items with
different \fB\%Item#group\fRs never share a group, and an item whose key
is the prefix itself (\fB\%git\fR in \fB\%git\fR) is a member like the others.
Groups and items are sorted by prefix or key ignoring case, items of
one key in item order.
.PP
Rows are named relative to their group: in \fB\%abrt\-action\fR, the group
\fB\%abrt\-action\-analyze\fR is \fB\%analyze\fR and the item \fB\%abrt\-action\-notify(1)\fR
is \fB\%notify(1)\fR. An item named like its group is named relative to
the group above (\fB\%abrt(1)\fR in \fB\%abrt\fR, \fB\%dump(1)\fR in \fB\%abrt\-dump\fR), and
one whose label does not start with the group prefix keeps its whole
label.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBINDENT = 2\fR
Columns each nesting level indents.
.TP 4
\fBMIN_GROUP = 3\fR
Fewest items that make a group.
.TP 4
\fBSEPARATORS = {\(aq\-\(aq, \(aq_\(aq, \(aq.\(aq, \(aq:\(aq, \(aq/\(aq}\fR
Characters that end a name token.
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.PP
\fBdef self.new(items : Array(Item))\fR
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.each_token(key : String, & : Int32, Int32 \-> ) : Nil\fR
Calls the block with the token boundaries of \fIkey\fR: the end of the
token (the end of its prefix) and the start of the next token.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.relative(text : String, outer : String, above : String = "") : Tuple(String, Int32)\fR
\fItext\fR (a prefix or a label) relative to the group prefix \fIouter\fR:
without \fIouter\fR and the separators after it, and the characters
dropped. Text that does not continue \fIouter\fR with a separator and
more name (\fB\%abrt\-dump(1)\fR in \fB\%abrt\-dump\fR) is relative to \fIabove\fR,
the prefix of the group around that one; text that does not start
with \fIouter\fR is whole.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef items(id : Int32) : Array(Int32)\fR
The items under node \fIid\fR, in outline order.
.TP 4
\fBdef leaf(index : Int32) : Int32\fR
The node id of item \fIindex\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef nodes : Array(Docv::Viewer::Picker::Outline::Node)\fR
Every node; a group comes before its children.
.TP 4
\fBdef roots : Array(Int32)\fR
Top\-level node ids, in item group order, then outline order.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/viewer/outline.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "Docv::Viewer::Picker" (3cr),
